# Ethos-U Smoke Test

`geisa-ethosu-smoke-test` is a host-side development diagnostic. It is not a
GEISA application, a managed application, or a performance benchmark.

The helper uses the Apache-2.0 TensorFlow Lite MobileNet example and Grace
Hopper image installed by the release-selected `tensorflow-lite` package. It
checks the source model SHA-256, uses Vela for `ethos-u65-256` to create a
temporary compiled model, loads `/usr/lib/libethosu_delegate.so`, and runs one
inference through `/dev/ethosu0`. It succeeds only when the delegate reports
at least one delegated graph node and the expected result is returned.

When you run `geisa-ethosu-smoke-test --profile /platform/profiles/nxp-ethosu-tflite`,
the helper applies the profile's declared `pythonpath` and `library-path`,
uses the profile's own `libethosu_delegate.so`, suppresses Python bytecode
writes, and reports the resolved module and library paths that were loaded.

The CLI reports the compiled-model path and SHA-256, delegated-node evidence,
the expected and actual result, elapsed time, and a final `PASS` or `FAIL`.

All generated files are removed when the command exits. It requires no network
access and does not start an LXC container or modify application state.

Run:

    geisa-ethosu-smoke-test
    geisa-ethosu-smoke-test --profile /platform/profiles/nxp-ethosu-tflite

Use `--verbose` to include Vela output. The exact example model, input, and
their declared source provenance are provided by the TensorFlow Lite recipe.
